{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374272-order-themed-imbued-items","id":1374272,"title":"Order Themed Imbued Items","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-11T18:55:27-07:00","id":1374272,"title":"Order Themed Imbued Items","content":"A game I was in had planned out a set of Imbued Items to give to the Pentacle Orders, one for each Order. Unfortunately, the game wrapped up before crafting could finish, so I'm sharing so that they don't go to waste. For context: these were designed through the lense of a Mage whose symbolism was inspired by the reverse-Buddhism of &quot;Kill 600 Billion Demon&quot; and acknowledge four fundamental &quot;laws&quot;: Flame Law, Blood Law, Sword Law and Corpse Law.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the Silver Ladder a back-mounted Lunargent Ladder (with 9 rungs and 3 rails per numerology) that embodies the enlightenment of Flame, the blaze of one's own innate divinity. It is to know one's self is a self-imposed delusion without losing hold upon the substance of that delusion. Death is used to perfect the nimbus of the soul. Matter is used to enhance the ladder as a status symbol. Spirit (supplemented by Death) is used to look into Twilight and Shadow, which also uses the nature of Lunargent. Time grants mental acceleration, planning outside the delusion of existence.<br /> <br /> For the Guardians of the Veil a hooded cloak woven from the perfected material of dead cut off human hair (a mix from 70 different people, due to numerology) that embodies the enlightenment of Corpse Law found in the suicidal nihlism and isolation of the Demiurge and drawing upon the latent divine power soaked into the Demiurge's corpse. From Death comes animation of the hair, sending out whisps and tufts and thin strands that the owner can feel and touch through (blindly groping at the world). Matter allows these strands to cause solid materials to ripple away from them and let them pass. Spirit grants the ability to curse with gremlins. Time grants that actions taken while the hood is up take place in an alternate time line that never actually occurs. Nothing the wearer does matters<br /> <br /> For the Adamantine Arrow, an arrow of adamantine (perfected glass) with a 4 edged arrow head (numerology) that embodies the enlightenment of Sword Law, the art of severing and cutting, which the Demiurge wielded against itself in its divine suicide. Time will cleave cause from effect, allowing the wielder to fire the arrow again and again without ever losing hold of it. Matter both enhances the cutting edge of arrowhead and ensures nothing can mar the nigh-invisibility of the arrow. Death is where things get interesting, as it is used to Perfect the entropic destructive act of the arrow cleaving through things. Flesh and sympathetic bonds alike are sundered. That which is cut open by its path cannot be mended without magic. Additionally Death is used to &quot;self annihilate&quot; the wielder when they are about to loose the arrow, making the person absent from the act of firing the arrow. In other words negating dice penalties originating from the wielder<br /> <br /> For the Free Council a smart phone case of perfected plastic (with 3 physical buttons or 12 if you count the electronic buttons. Numerology!) that embodies the enlightenment Blood Law found in the links and interconnections of the world, binding oneself to the community and the flaming souls of others. Unlike the other items this is not meant to be wielded by a mage, but instead a Sleepwalker. Furthermore the phone itself can be swapped and upgraded within the case. Time grants the wielder the ability to Alter History gaining and discarding Status, Allies, Contacts, Resources, and Retainers. Time also allows the manipulation of temporal sympathy. Matter enhances the smartphone as a tool of communication and research. If somebody answers a call made from the contained phone, Spirit allows the wielder the ability to talk with the spirit of the answerer's group or organization or the building containing the phone. Death grants the wielder knowledge of social decay and the weak points that will cause a group to fall apart<br /> <br /> For the Mysterium, a book rendered into a puzzle box, made of perfected Tin Amalgam (mystery and enlightenment). Where the other objects provide an answer to &quot;What is the path to enlightenment?&quot; this is meant to ask the question. The book acts as a library of stored impressions of Numina, Influences and ephemeral entities from any that it encounters or ever could have encountered in alternate histories. Also furthermore Matter collates information from material data stores that the book encounters or ever could have encountered. To access this vast store of information the puzzle must be solved, because this process constructs a temporary ghost of a future of the solver that spent their time studying the book. The ghost is bound to the book and acts as a guide, index, and firewall against abyssal influence. The puzzle thus has a different unique solution configuration for each solver but each solution configuration requires 30 steps (numerology)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}